= Code line options

Line numbers and highlighted lines are attributes on the line above a fence. The engine passes them to `<pre>` unchanged; the highlighter reads them.

{.line-numbers data-line-start=40 data-highlight=3,6-7}
```php "src/Invoice.php"
final class Invoice
{
    public function total(): Money
    {
        $sum = Money::zero($this->currency);
        foreach ($this->lines as $line) {
            $sum = $sum->add($line->amount());
        }

        return $sum;
    }
}
```
^ An excerpt that starts at line 40 of its file, with three lines marked.

Highlight only, no gutter:

{data-highlight=2}
```js
const total = lines.reduce((sum, line) => sum + line.amount, 0);
console.log(total);
```

Line numbers only, counted from 1:

{.line-numbers}
```sh
composer require markup-carve/carve-php
vendor/bin/carve render README.crv
```
